        {
          "headline": "UK publishes a transparency record for five machine-learning reoffending predictors used in sentencing",
          "sources": [
            { "name": "GOV.UK", "url": "https://www.gov.uk/algorithmic-transparency-records/hmpps-risk-of-reoffending-tools" }
          ],
          "bullets": [
            "The record, published on 19 November under the Algorithmic Transparency Recording Standard at version 4.0, covers five machine-learning sub-tools used by HM Prison and Probation Service in England and Wales: the All Reoffending Predictor, Violent Reoffending Predictor, Serious Violent Reoffending Predictor, Combined Serious Reoffending Predictor and Sexual Reoffending Predictor. Each gives a risk score estimating the likelihood of proven reoffending within two years.",
            "The record states the tools are used during sentencing in court and for risk assessment in prison and on probation, feeding pre-sentence reports, Risk of Serious Harm assessments, community supervision levels and allocation to intervention programmes; police use the sexual-reoffending sub-tool for individuals with notification requirements. The record says the scores \"support, rather than automate, practitioners' individual-level risk judgements\".",
