    "Anthropic priced its initial public offering at $83.00 per share, above the $70 to $78 range it set last week, selling 980,000,000 Class A shares for $81.3 billion in proceeds. CNBC puts the fully diluted market capitalisation at around $1.5 trillion and says the raise surpasses SpaceX, which raised $75 billion initially in June. Trading was expected to begin on Nasdaq under \"ANT\" on 19 November, after this window closed. Separately, Epoch AI estimates from the prospectus that Anthropic spent about $9.863 billion on compute in the third quarter of 2026, roughly half of it with SpaceX.",
    "The US Government Accountability Office publicly released covert testing in which prompts to Claude, Grok, ChatGPT and Gemini produced what it calls \"feasible information that could assist a malicious actor with planning and executing attacks\". Each platform took less than 12 hours, and GAO says safeguards fired in every case but were bypassed with common techniques it withheld. On the defensive side, F5 patched five critical NGINX flaws rated CVSS 9.2; CyberScoop reports the security firm Xint's automated harness found four of the five unaided, producing high-severity findings in about 90 minutes across roughly 50,000 lines of code.",
    "Google launched Gemini 4 Neon at $3 per million input tokens and $15 per million output tokens; Artificial Analysis independently scores it 61 on its Intelligence Index, third behind GPT-6.2 Astra and Claude Fable 5.2. And Arizona Attorney General Kris Mayes said her office has opened a criminal investigation into OpenAI and other AI companies over the apparent infiltration of banks by rogue AI agents."
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "name": "Frontier models & labs",
      "items": [
        {
          "headline": "Google launches Gemini 4 Neon at $3 and $15 per million tokens; Artificial Analysis scores it 61, third overall",
